# Database Schema Rule (Must Follow)

- Use the user-provided NHUTIN schema as the only source of truth for database structure.
- Do not invent, rename, or assume table/column names.
- Before writing SQL/PHP queries, map fields exactly to the schema:
  - `customers.company_name` (not `name`)
  - `customers.notes` (not `note`)
  - `customers.customer_type_id` (not `customer_type`)
  - `customers.logo_url` (not `avatar_url`)
- If a required field/mapping is unclear, ask the user first instead of guessing.
- For customer CRUD, keep compatibility with current schema and constraints (including FKs and enum status values).
- Prefer explicit, schema-aligned error messages when SQL fails.
